      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This issue is likely caused by a restricted air duct serving that specific room, such as a blocked vent, a partially closed flange, or debris inside the ductwork. It could also stem from the thermostat being installed in that room and failing to override the system aggressively to lower the temperature locally. Finally, if the room is negatively pressurized compared to the rest of the home due to an HVAC leak or cracked registers nearby, heated or humid air may be leaking back into it, preventing cooling despite the unit running constantly.",
