      "content": "It is possible that a loosen metal standpipe, debris inside a register sleeve, or a disconnected connection exists deep within the vent run and isn't visible from the accessible path. Even a small amount of insulation misplaced inside an air plenum or between joists can create significant resistance, forcing the system to blow much cooler air than the unit is capable of delivering into that one airspace. This hidden restriction effectively turns your AC into a constant fan when it tries to push air through the blockage. Having a specialist inspect the duct interior is often the only way to confirm if something unseen is creating this physical resistance.",
